  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seminar follow-up of Horticulture Centre of Excellene (CeO) in Kenya (MAT16KE01)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The study mainly aimed to identify if there is enough common ground to start setting up a CoE in Kenya. The first objective of this study was to investigate the interest in the Dutch and Kenyan horticulture sector to further cooperation and the potential to realize this through the establishment of a CoE. The second objective was to review examples of centres of excellence in developing economies with Dutch involvement and research the manners to come to advise for the best suitable, financially sustainable business model(s) for a CoE in Kenya. This seminar is the first step in giving follow-up to this study. Dutch and Kenyan stakeholders are interested in a CoE. This seminar was the first step to discuss further activities towards a CoE and cooperation within the horticulture sector.</narrative>
  </description>
